           folder even in a Release build. The closing check stays: xcopy exits 0
           on a wildcard miss, so a missing DLL is silent here and the exe then
           dies at startup with 0xC06D007E, Targetcore being delay-loaded. -->
      <Command>xcopy /Y "..\..\..\bin\$(Configuration)64\Msgcore.dll" "$(OutDir)"
if exist "..\..\..\bin\$(Configuration)64\Msgcore.pdb" xcopy /Y "..\..\..\bin\$(Configuration)64\Msgcore.pdb" "$(OutDir)"
xcopy /Y "..\..\..\bin\$(Configuration)64\Targetcore.dll" "$(OutDir)"
if exist "..\..\..\bin\$(Configuration)64\Targetcore.pdb" xcopy /Y "..\..\..\bin\$(Configuration)64\Targetcore.pdb" "$(OutDir)"
if not exist "$(OutDir)Targetcore.dll" echo POSTBUILD ERROR: Targetcore.dll not found in "..\..\..\bin\$(Configuration)64" -- build Targetcore first. &amp;&amp; exit /b 1</Command>
    </PostBuildEvent>
